                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "As a creator's first major project, it's fine. But this is far from good. The lack of settings and way too high sensitivity is a nightmare, the puzzles are nonsensical and just assumes you know mechanics (typing without a dialogue prompt to say something), the level select is just \"remember the name of this level,\" and you need to verify files every single time to get an achievement. \n\nIt's free. It's a mess, but at least it's free. And counts to Steam profile achievements if you enjoy those. But just for fun? This is not a fun experience.",
